<title>HUNGARY: Budapest BSE to start continuous index.</title>
<headline>Budapest BSE to start continuous index.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Budapest Stock Exchange (BSE) said on Friday that it would start the continuous calculation of the BUX index on April 1.</p>
<p>In addition to continuous calculation the BSE will also publish the opening, the daily low and high values of the BUX index, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Currently the BUX index is calculated once a day, following of the close of trade.</p>
<p>As an additional change the official daily BUX index will be calculated based on closing prices instead of the current system when the BUX index is calculated from average prices, it said.</p>
<p>Also effective April 1, the BUX index basket is changing. The bourse drops Domus, Dunaholding and Styl but adds Horizon-Multiplan.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
